---
title: How to Set Default Invoice Items
description: >-
  Save ready-made line items in your invoice settings, then add them to any
  invoice or quotation from the editor with one click.
sidebar:
  order: 19
---
**Default items are ready-made invoice lines, such as a setup fee or an hourly rate. Save them once in your settings, then add them to any invoice from the editor, the same way you add a service.**

### **Add Default Items**

1. Go to **Settings → Invoice Settings**.
1. Open the **Default Items** tab.
1. Click **Add Item**.
1. Fill in the item:
   - **Title** – the name of the line, for example *Setup fee*.
   - **Description** – what the line covers.
   - **Quantity** – the quantity to start with. The default is `1`.
   - **Price** – the price for one unit.
1. Click **Save Changes**.

A line needs a **Title** or a **Description**. Quantity and price must be zero or more. You can keep up to **50** default items.

### **Edit or Delete an Item**

The tab lists your items in a table with **Title**, **Description**, **Quantity**, **Price** and **Actions**.

- Click the **pencil** icon on a row to change the item, then click **Save Changes**.
- Click the **trash** icon to delete it, then confirm.

Every add, edit and delete is saved straight away. There is no separate save button for the list.

### **Add a Default Item to an Invoice**

1. Open an invoice and click **Edit Invoice**.
1. Under the items, click **From Default Items**, next to **From Services**.
1. Click the item you want.

The item is added as a normal line. You can change its title, description, quantity and price on the invoice. The saved default stays as it was.

{% table %}
---
- **Tip:** The **From Default Items** button only appears once you have saved at least one default item.
{% /table %}

### **Quotations Too**

**Settings → Quotation Settings** has the same **Default Items** tab, with its own list. Invoices and quotations do not share items. In the quotation editor, use **From Default Items** the same way.

### **Good to Know**

- Changing a default item does not change invoices that already use it.
- If you have the editor open while you change your defaults, reload the page to see the new list.
